Cmn1=MODULE NAME: 	{{**{{CP}}**}} Astronomical Lighting Control\\CATEGORY: 	Lighting\\
Cmn2=\\AUTHOR:  	Chris Cates, CAIP\\COMPANY: 	Creative Programming Inc.
Cmn3=||1\\	 	(www.creativeprogramming.ca)\\\\VERSION: 	1.00 (2012-03-16)\\
Cmn4=\\SUMMARY: \\Automated Lighting On/Off Control based on Longitude||1
Cmn5=& Latitude with optional sunrise/sunset delay timers and early morning/late||1
Cmn6=night on/off controls.\\\\MODULE DESCRIPTION:\\This module simplifies||1
Cmn7=Crestron's Astronomical Clock symbol and groups all necessary symbols||1
Cmn8=to automate outdoor lights turning on & off with sunrise and sunset.
Cmn9=||2\\\\This module allows for a customizable delay to have the lights||1
Cmn10=turn on prior to sunset and after sunrise.  This module also allows||1
Cmn11=for the lights to be turned off at a specific time late at night||1
Cmn12=and turned back on again in the early morning to prevent lights||1
Cmn13=from staying on all night and using unecessary energy.  \\\\Use||1
Cmn14=the following web site to help get the necessary Longitude & Latitude||1
Cmn15=parameters: http://itouchmap.com/latlong.html\\Use a weather web||1
Cmn16=site like http://weather.yahoo.com to help get the correct sunrise||1
Cmn17=and sunset for the specified city.  By adjusting the time on your||1
Cmn18=processor you can verify the lights turning on/off at the correct||1
Cmn19=times.  \\\\\\INPUT DESCRIPTIONS: \\\\Name                   Type	
Cmn20=Description\\----------------------------------------\\Initialize	
Cmn21=		D	Pulse at system startup to load parameters\\{{**{{Test_Lights_On/Off}}**}}	
Cmn22=D	Pulse to test outdoor lights turning on/off\\					These signals||1
Cmn23=are optional\\\\OUTPUT DESCRIPTIONS: \\\\Name||C
Cmn24=Type	Description\\----------------------------------------\\Lights_On/Off}}**}}	
Cmn25=	D	Pulses at specified times (see parameters) to turn\\					lights||1
Cmn26=on/off\\PARAMETERS: \\\\Name			Description\\--------------------
Cmn27=--------------------\\Latitude-Degrees	Numerical value for geographical||1
Cmn28=latitude degree\\			(Valid values range from 0 to 180)\\Latitude-
Cmn29=Minutes	Numerical value for geographical latitude minutes\\			(Valid||1
Cmn30=values range from 0 to 90)\\Latitude-Is-North	Select Yes if geographical||1
Cmn31=location is in\\ 			northern hemisphere\\\\Latitude-Degrees	Numerical||1
Cmn32=value for geographical longitude degree\\			(Valid values range||1
Cmn33=from 0 to 180)\\Latitude-Minutes	Numerical value for geographical||1
Cmn34=longitude minutes\\			(Valid values range from 0 to 90)\\Longitude-
Cmn35=Is-East	Select Yes if geographical location is in\\ 			eastern hemisphere\\
Cmn36=\\GMT-Offset		Numerical value for Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) Offset\\
Cmn37=||1			for your time zone (Valid values range from -12 to 12)\\\\Sunrise-
Cmn38=Delay	Number of minutes after sunrise lights will turn off\\			(Valid||1
Cmn39=values range from 0 to 90)\\Sunset-Delay	Number of minutes prior||1
Cmn40=to sunset lights will turn on\\			(Valid values range from -0 to||1
Cmn41=-90)\\\\{{**{{Early-Morning-On}}**}}	Time lights will turn on in the morning\\
Cmn42=||1			Time must be entered in numerical format compatible with\\ 	
Cmn43=		When symbol (xx.xx.xx.xx). So to have lights turn on at\\ 			6:
Cmn44=35am the time will have to be entered as: 06.35.00.00s\\ 			(This||1
Cmn45=parameter is optional)\\\\{{**{{Late-Night-Off}}**}}	Time lights will turn||1
Cmn46=off at night\\ 			Time must be entered in numerical format compatible||1
Cmn47=with\\ 			When symbol (xx.xx.xx.xx). So to have lights turn off||1
Cmn48=at\\ 			11:50pm the time will have to be entered as: 23.50.00.00s\\
Cmn49=||1			(This parameter is optional)\\\\\\REVISION HISTORY:\\Ver-1.00||1
Cmn50=- Initial Release, 2012-02-16\\\\SUPPORT:\\No support or warranty||1
Cmn51=is given with the use of this module.  If you experience any problems||1
Cmn52=using this module please contact the author at: info@creativeprogramming.
Cmn53=ca\\\\COPYRIGHT INFORMATION:\\This module is the property of Creative||1
Cmn54=Programming Inc. and is distributed under the terms of the GNU General||1
Cmn55=Public License agreement.  Use and distribution of this module is||1
Cmn56=provided under the agreement that the orginal author is credited.
Cmn57=||1\\(c) 2012 - Creative Programming Inc.
